<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 20 February, from 1339 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mercenary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1339">1339 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">687 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Milanese defeat Lodrisio Visconti's mercenaries at Parabiago</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Parabiago, in deep snow, the exiled Lodrisio Visconti's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> Compagnia di San Giorgio routed part of the Milanese army and captured Luchino Visconti. The Milanese rallied, freed Luchino and defeated Lodrisio.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1472">1472 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">554 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orkney and Shetland annexed to the Scottish crown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pledged by Christian I of Denmark-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> as security for his daughter's dowry when she married James III, the unredeemed islands were formally annexed by the Scottish Parliament.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1547">1547 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">479 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nine-year-old Edward VI is crowned</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s only son was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>. Under his regents <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> became firmly Protestant, but Edward died aged fifteen in 1553.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington signs the Postal Service Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The act established the US Post Office on a permanent footing and allowed newspapers to be mailed cheaply. It helped bind together a scattered young republic.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Union army suffers heavy losses at the Battle of Olustee</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Battle of Olustee, or Ocean Pond, in Baker County near Lake City, the Union army suffered a casualty rate of one in three. It was the largest battle fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1872">1872 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">154 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Metropolitan Museum of Art opens in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The museum opened in a former dance academy on Fifth Avenue with a modest collection. It moved to Central Park in 1880 and grew into one of the world's largest art museums.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1962">1962 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Glenn becomes the first American to orbit Earth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aboard Friendship 7, Glenn circled the Earth three times in under five hours. Ten months after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuri-gagarin">Yuri Gagarin</a>'s flight, it restored American confidence in the space race.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1986">1986 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">40 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union launches the core of the Mir space station</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mir's first module was launched from Baikonur. Expanded over ten years, the station hosted crews from many nations and was continuously occupied for almost a decade before its re-entry in 2001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 20 February <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francesco-maria-ii-della-rovere"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francesco-maria-ii-della-rovere.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francesco Maria II della Rovere</span><span class="tp">1549–1631</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-alexandre-berthier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-alexandre-berthier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis-Alexandre Berthier</span><span class="tp">1753–1815</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-naguib"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muhammad-naguib.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Muhammad Naguib</span><span class="tp">1901–1984</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/forbes-burnham"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/forbes-burnham.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Forbes Burnham</span><span class="tp">1923–1985</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 20 February <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yaroslav-the-wise.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yaroslav the Wise</span><span class="tp">c. 978–1054</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/conan-iv-duke-of-brittany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/conan-iv-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Conan IV, Duke of Brittany</span><span class="tp">c. 1138–1171</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tancred-king-of-sicily"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tancred-king-of-sicily.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tancred, King of Sicily</span><span class="tp">c. 1138–1194</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-martin-v"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-martin-v.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Martin V</span><span class="tp">1369–1431</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tecun-uman"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tecun-uman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tecun Uman</span><span class="tp">d. 1524</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-emmanuel-iii-of-sardinia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-emmanuel-iii-of-sardinia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles Emmanuel III of Sardinia</span><span class="tp">1701–1773</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andreas-hofer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andreas-hofer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andreas Hofer</span><span class="tp">1767–1810</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-douglass"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Frederick Douglass</span><span class="tp">c. 1818–1895</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sadri-maqsudi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sadri-maqsudi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sadri Maqsudi</span><span class="tp">1878–1957</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
